# Move to Uncoil from another tool

You do not need a big migration. Send traces to Uncoil while your current tool keeps running, compare a week of runs, then remove the old tool.

## The plan

1. Create an Uncoil project and copy its API key.
2. Add the Uncoil SDK ([TypeScript](/docs/typescript) or [Python](/docs/python)), or point an OpenTelemetry exporter at Uncoil.
3. Run your agent. Check that each run shows its model calls, tool calls, cost and errors.
4. After a week of matching results, turn the old tool off.

Uncoil receives traces after the work is done, so it is never in your request path.

## If you already use OpenTelemetry

Send OTLP HTTP JSON to `https://eu.cloud.uncoil.dev/api/otel` with the project API key. Most setups only change the endpoint and the key. See [OpenTelemetry and integrations](/docs/integrations).

## Coming from another tool

If your current tool takes OpenTelemetry over HTTP, change the endpoint and key and keep the rest. Export anything you need before you turn it off, and see "Bring old traces with you" below for moving history.

## Coming from LangSmith

Replace the LangSmith tracing variables with an OpenTelemetry exporter that points at Uncoil. LangChain and LangGraph code stays as it is; only the destination of the traces changes. Run both side by side for a week, then turn LangSmith off.

## Coming from Helicone

Add the Uncoil SDK or an OpenTelemetry exporter to your agent code. If you use Helicone as a gateway for routing and fallbacks, keep it and remove only the logging you no longer need. Check that tool calls now show inside each run.

## Bring old traces with you

Old traces can follow through the [Ingestion API](/docs/api). Send each one with its original `createdAt` and a stable `spanId` and `runId` built from the old record id, so running the import twice creates no duplicates. Runs show on their original dates.

Your plan's retention still applies: data older than the plan keeps (7, 30 or 90 days) is removed each night, so older imports do not stay. Try about 20 runs first and check their dates in the dashboard. Cost stays at zero unless you supply a rate card.

## What does not move

Datasets, prompts and scores have no bulk import. Recreate the important ones in Uncoil. Keep your old tool read-only for as long as you want the rest of its history.

## Check your bill first

The [tracing bill calculator](https://www.uncoil.dev/tools/ai-observability-cost-calculator) compares the monthly cost on each tool for your own traffic. The [Switch to Uncoil](https://www.uncoil.dev/switch) page has the same steps with comparison links.
